{"id":"n-20261021-wcccob","category":"gaming","display_title":"Counter-Strike Pro Faces Tax Fraud Charges","display_title_he":"שחקן קונטר-סטרייק מקצועי עומד בפני אישומי עבירות מס","short_summary":"Professional Counter-Strike 2 player Aleksi “Aleksib” Virolainen is facing a suspended prison sentence in Finland over undeclared virtual sticker revenue.","english_level":"C1","words":412,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"IGN","domain":"ign.com","url":"https://www.ign.com/articles/counter-strike-2-pro-aleksib-faces-four-month-suspended-prison-sentence-over-charges-of-aggravated-tax-fraud","title":"Counter-Strike 2 Pro Aleksib Faces Four-Month Suspended Prison Sentence Over Charges of Aggravated Tax Fraud","published_at":"2026-10-20T22:45:55.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-20T22:45:55.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-21T06:19:36.038Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The professional gaming world has found itself entangled in an unexpected legal dispute as a prominent esports competitor faces potential prison time over taxation issues. According to reports, Aleksi “Aleksib” Virolainen, a well-known Counter-Strike 2 professional player currently representing Natus Vincere, is confronting a possible four-month suspended prison sentence in Finland. The legal proceedings stem from allegations of aggravated tax fraud relating to earnings generated from virtual in-game items.","Legal documents outlined during a court session at the Eastern Uusimaa District Court reveal that the controversy centers around financial compensation received from Valve, the developer of the game. Prosecutors allege that during 2020, specifically between May 19 and September 22 in Vantaa, Virolainen failed to declare approximately €53,000 in income derived from virtual sticker sales. In the ecosystem of Counter-Strike 2, players frequently acquire digital stickers to customize weapons through the Steam Marketplace, the CS2 Store, capsules, or third-party websites. Professional competitors often secure a share of the revenue generated through these marketplace transactions and other in-game purchases when they compete at major tournaments.","Authorities assert that by omitting these specific earnings from his financial declarations, the player successfully avoided paying an estimated €28,000 in applicable taxes. Furthermore, prosecutors pointed out that a subpoena stated that a pre-filled tax return form for the 2019 year was never returned, and the missing Valve revenues were omitted entirely from his official filings.","During the court appearance, which drew considerable attention across the competitive gaming community after a tweet containing footage of him arriving at court went viral, Virolainen entered a plea of not guilty to the charges brought against him. The defense argued that at the time of the alleged incidents, the player was only 22 years old and possessed no real understanding of how the tax system worked. Representatives maintained that because taxes had already been taken out of his general income, he operated under the assumption that his taxes had been fully handled, emphasizing that no financial gain was sought through the omission.","Although the indictment has been formally read, a definitive district court ruling regarding the case has yet to be issued, meaning the now-29-year-old player has not been formally convicted of any crime. As the legal process continues to unfold, Virolainen remains an active competitor in the esports arena, having previously competed at two Majors with ENCE during that era—including a notable finish at the IEM Katowice 2019 Major where his team reached the Grand Finals—while officials prepare to deliver their final verdict at a later date."],"facts":[{"fact":"Aleksi “Aleksib” Virolainen is facing a four-month suspended prison sentence over alleged aggravated tax fraud in Finland.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The charges involve failing to declare €53,000 in income from Valve earned through in-game sticker sales in 2020.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Prosecutors claim he avoided paying approximately €28,000 in taxes.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Virolainen pleaded not guilty, stating he was 22 at the time, lacked understanding of the tax system, and believed his taxes were handled.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"An indictment was read at the Eastern Uusimaa District Court, and a ruling will be issued at a later date.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Virolainen is currently 29 years old and represents Natus Vincere as an active Counter-Strike 2 player.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"professional","lemma":"professional","pos":"adjective","he":"מקצועי","name":false},{"text":"gaming","lemma":"gaming","pos":"noun","he":"גיימינג","name":false},{"text":"world","lemma":"world","pos":"noun","he":"עולם","name":false},{"text":"has found itself","lemma":"find oneself","pos":"verb","he":"מצא את עצמו","name":false},{"text":"entangled","lemma":"entangled","pos":"adjective","he":"מסובך","name":false},{"text":"unexpected","lemma":"unexpected","pos":"adjective","he":"בלתי צפוי","name":false},{"text":"legal","lemma":"legal","pos":"adjective","he":"משפטי","name":false},{"text":"dispute","lemma":"dispute","pos":"noun","he":"סכסוך","name":false},{"text":"prominent","lemma":"prominent","pos":"adjective","he":"בכיר / בולט","name":false},{"text":"esports","lemma":"esports","pos":"noun","he":"ספורט אלקטרוני","name":false},{"text":"competitor","lemma":"competitor","pos":"noun","he":"מתחרה","name":false},{"text":"faces","lemma":"face","pos":"verb","he":"עומד בפני","name":false},{"text":"potential","lemma":"potential","pos":"adjective","he":"פוטנציאלי","name":false},{"text":"prison","lemma":"prison","pos":"noun","he":"כלא","name":false},{"text":"time","lemma":"time","pos":"noun","he":"זמן","name":false},{"text":"taxation","lemma":"taxation","pos":"noun","he":"מיסוי","name":false},{"text":"issues","lemma":"issue","po